      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a bathroom renovation cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A bathroom remodel in Bainbridge Island typically ranges from 15,000 to 20,000 for entry-level updates, 25,000 to 30,000 for average renovations, and 50,000 to 60,000 for higher-end work. Costs depend on layout changes and material selections."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a bathroom renovation usually take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most renovations take one to two weeks once work begins. For standard layouts, a one-day remodel option may be available. The timeline depends on layout adjustments and material availability.\u00a0"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is included in a full bathroom renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A full renovation typically includes layout updates, shower or tub changes, flooring, lighting, ventilation, and finish upgrades that improve usability and reduce clutter."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need permits for a bathroom renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Permit requirements depend on the scope. Plumbing or mechanical changes may require permits, and applications are typically handled through the city\u2019s permit system before work begins."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I stay in my home during the renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In most cases, yes. The level of disruption depends on how many bathrooms are available and how the work is staged."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What should I upgrade first in a bathroom renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Start with layout and lighting. These have the biggest impact on how the room feels and how easily it can be maintained."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it better to renovate the full bathroom at once or in phases?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Renovating at once usually produces a more consistent result. Phasing can make it harder to align layout and lighting improvements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I choose the right bathroom layout?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Focus on circulation and wall use. A layout that reduces congestion will make the space easier to use."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the best materials for bathroom walls and floors?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Moisture-resistant materials with fewer seams help reduce buildup and simplify cleaning."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What type of flooring works best in a bathroom?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Slip-resistant, water-tolerant flooring that dries quickly is ideal."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I choose a shower or bathtub for my space?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Consider daily use. Showers often improve flow, while tubs may still be needed depending on the household."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a tub-to-shower conversion worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It can be, especially when the tub is rarely used. Conversions often free up space and simplify upkeep."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I improve bathroom ventilation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Installing an effective exhaust fan helps remove humidity and keeps surfaces drier."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a bathroom renovation increase home value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, especially when layout and usability improvements make the space easier to maintain."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What bathroom upgrades give the best return on investment?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Layout improvements, better showers, and improved ventilation typically provide the strongest value."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I balance style and function in a bathroom renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Start with layout and usability, then choose finishes that support the design."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are the most common mistakes in bathroom renovations?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
